msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Governance\n"
"\n"
"This document describes the governance structure of the project, including decision-making processes, roles and responsibilities, and community behavior guidelines.\n"
"\n"
"## Roles and Responsibilities\n"
"\n"
"### Maintainers\n"
"Maintainers are responsible for the overall direction and health of the project. Their duties include:\n"
"- Reviewing and merging or rejecting pull requests\n"
"- Managing project releases and versioning\n"
"- Resolving disputes and making final decisions when consensus cannot be reached\n"
"- Ensuring the project adheres to its technical roadmap\n"
"- Maintaining a welcoming and productive community environment\n"
"\n"
"### Committers\n"
"Committers have write access to the repository and are responsible for:\n"
"- Reviewing pull requests and providing constructive feedback\n"
"- Merging approved pull requests\n"
"- Maintaining code quality and test coverage\n"
"- Assisting contributors with their submissions\n"
"\n"
"### Contributors\n"
"Contributors are community members who submit pull requests, report issues, or participate in discussions. They are expected to:\n"
"- Follow the project's contribution guidelines\n"
"- Respect the code of conduct\n"
"- Engage constructively in discussions\n"
"\n"
"## Decision-Making Process\n"
"\n"
"### Consensus-Based Decision Making\n"
"The project uses a consensus-based decision-making process. For most decisions, maintainers work together to reach consensus. When consensus cannot be reached, a vote may be called.\n"
"\n"
"### Voting\n"
"- Each maintainer has one vote\n"
"- A simple majority is required for most decisions\n"
"- For significant changes (e.g., changes to the governance model, major architectural changes), a two-thirds majority is required\n"
"- Voting periods last a minimum of 72 hours\n"
"\n"
"### Request for Comments (RFC)\n"
"Significant changes or new features should go through the RFC process:\n"
"1. Submit an RFC document describing the proposed change\n"
"2. The RFC is discussed by the community for a minimum of 7 days\n"
"3. Maintainers vote on the RFC\n"
"4. If approved, the RFC is implemented\n"
"\n"
"## Code of Conduct\n"
"\n"
"All community members are expected to:\n"
"- Be respectful and inclusive\n"
"- Use welcoming and inclusive language\n"
"- Show empathy towards other community members\n"
"- Provide constructive feedback\n"
"- Focus on what is best for the community\n"
"\n"
"Unacceptable behavior includes:\n"
"- Harassment or discrimination of any kind\n"
"- Personal attacks or trolling\n"
"- Publishing others' private information without consent\n"
"- Any other conduct that could reasonably be considered inappropriate in a professional setting\n"
"\n"
"## Conflict Resolution\n"
"\n"
"When conflicts arise:\n"
"1. The parties involved should first attempt to resolve the issue directly\n"
"2. If resolution is not possible, a maintainer may be asked to mediate\n"
"3. If the conflict persists, the maintainers will make a final decision\n"
"\n"
"## Changes to Governance\n"
"\n"
"Changes to this governance document require:\n"
"- A proposal submitted to the community\n"
"- A minimum 7-day discussion period\n"
"- A two-thirds majority vote of maintainers\n"
"\n"
"## Attribution\n"
"\n"
"This governance model is inspired by best practices from the open-source community and may be adapted as the project evolves.\n"

msgid "治理机制"
msgstr "Governance mechanism"

msgid "使命"
msgstr "Mission"

msgid "作为 Triton 生态的重要组成部分，Triton-Ascend 项目致力于为所有昇腾 NPU 用户提供高效易用的 Triton 编译框架，使 Triton 代码能够在昇腾硬件上高效运行，并积极贡献于丰富 Triton 和昇腾生态。"
msgstr "As an important part of the Triton ecosystem, the Triton-Ascend project is committed to providing an efficient and easy-to-use Triton compilation framework for all Ascend NPU users, enabling Triton code to run efficiently on Ascend hardware, and actively contributing to enriching the Triton and Ascend ecosystems."

msgid "原则"
msgstr "Principles"

msgid "**开放透明**：所有技术决策和社区讨论均通过公开渠道进行"
msgstr "**Openness and Transparency**: All technical decisions and community discussions are conducted through public channels."

msgid "**贡献导向**：成员资格基于个人能力和贡献，而非与雇主绑定"
msgstr "**Contribution-Oriented**: Membership is based on individual capability and contribution, rather than being tied to an employer."

msgid "**社区驱动**：鼓励广泛参与，尊重多元观点，通过讨论和投票达成共识"
msgstr "**Community-Driven**: Broad participation is encouraged, diverse perspectives are respected, and consensus is reached through discussion and voting."

msgid "治理结构"
msgstr "Governance structure"

msgid "Triton-Ascend 是 Triton 社区下的开源项目，角色任命最终由 Triton 社区决定。项目采用分层技术治理结构："
msgstr "Triton-Ascend is an open-source project under the Triton community, and role appointments are ultimately determined by the Triton community. The project adopts a layered technical governance structure:"

msgid "贡献者"
msgstr "Contributors"

msgid "**职责**："
msgstr "**Responsibilities**:"

msgid "帮助新贡献者融入项目"
msgstr "Help new contributors integrate into the project."

msgid "处理和回应社区 `Issue`"
msgstr "Handle and respond to community `Issue`s."

msgid "审阅 `RFC` 和代码"
msgstr "Review `RFC` and code."

msgid "**要求**："
msgstr "**Requirements**:"

msgid "完成至少一次贡献"
msgstr "Complete at least one contribution."

msgid "通过提交 `Issue`、代码评审、代码提交和参与社区活动等方式持续积极参与项目"
msgstr "Continue to actively participate in the project by submitting `Issues`, conducting code reviews, making code commits, and engaging in community activities."

msgid "**权限**：授予 GitHub 仓库 `Triage` 角色，包括读取和克隆权限，以及提交 Issue 和 PR 的权限。"
msgstr "**Permissions**: Grant the `Triage` role to the GitHub repository, including read and clone permissions, as well as permission to submit Issues and PRs."

msgid "Maintainer"
msgstr "Maintainer"

msgid "定义项目的愿景和使命，塑造技术方向，确保长期成功"
msgstr "Define the project's vision and mission, shape the technical direction, and ensure long-term success."

msgid "拥有代码合并权限，主导路线图规划"
msgstr "Has code merge permissions and leads roadmap planning."

msgid "审阅社区贡献并持续改进代码"
msgstr "Review community contributions and continuously improve the code."

msgid "负责核心模块的代码质量和架构决策"
msgstr "Responsible for code quality and architectural decisions of core modules."

msgid "参与发布决策"
msgstr "Participate in release decision-making."

msgid "指导贡献者完成代码贡献"
msgstr "Guide contributors through the process of making code contributions."

msgid "参与社区技术会议，讨论和投票技术方向、重大提案及 `Release` 事项"
msgstr "Participate in community technical meetings to discuss and vote on technical direction, major proposals, and `Release` matters."

msgid "对 Triton 和 Triton-Ascend 代码库有深入理解"
msgstr "Deep understanding of the Triton and Triton-Ascend codebases."

msgid "承诺持续代码贡献，具备设计、开发及 PR 审阅流程的能力"
msgstr "Committed to continuous code contribution, with the ability to design, develop, and review the PR process."

msgid "积极参与社区代码评审，至少交付一项重大功能，并保持持续高质量贡献"
msgstr "Actively participate in community code reviews, deliver at least one major feature, and maintain sustained high-quality contributions."

msgid "积极处理 `Issue`、回应咨询并参与讨论"
msgstr "Actively handle `Issue`s, respond to inquiries, and participate in discussions."

msgid "对项目做出重大技术贡献（如核心功能开发、架构设计、性能优化等）"
msgstr "Making significant technical contributions to the project (such as core feature development, architecture design, performance optimization, etc.)"

msgid "展现良好的技术判断力和社区协作能力"
msgstr "Demonstrate sound technical judgment and community collaboration skills."

msgid "**权限**：授予 GitHub 仓库写入权限，包括读取、克隆和推送代码权限，核心分支保护和合并权限，发布执行权限，以及管理 `Issue` 和 `Pull Request` 的权限。"
msgstr "**Permissions**: Grant write access to the GitHub repository, including permissions to read, clone, and push code, core branch protection and merge permissions, release execution permissions, and permissions to manage `Issues` and `Pull Requests`."

msgid "晋升由现有 `Maintainer` 共同评审，综合考虑贡献质量、连续性和社区参与度。"
msgstr "Promotion is jointly reviewed by existing `Maintainer`s, taking into account the quality of contributions, continuity, and community engagement."

msgid "提名与移除"
msgstr "Nomination and Removal"

msgid "成员资格基于个人能力，通过贡献、评审和讨论体现"
msgstr "Membership is based on individual capability, demonstrated through contributions, reviews, and discussions."

msgid "候选人需认同 Triton-Ascend 的原则并保持行为一致性"
msgstr "Candidates must identify with the principles of Triton-Ascend and maintain consistency in their behavior."

msgid "连续 **6 个月** 未对项目做出贡献的 `Maintainer` 可转为荣誉身份"
msgstr "A `Maintainer` who has not contributed to the project for **6 consecutive months** may be converted to honorary status."

msgid "成员资格授予个人，不与雇主绑定"
msgstr "Membership is granted to individuals and is not tied to their employer."

msgid "提名流程"
msgstr "Nomination Process"

msgid "任何人均可发起提名，包括自提名，通过社区 `Issue` 进行"
msgstr "Anyone can initiate a nomination, including self-nomination, through a community `Issue`."

msgid "提名须包含候选人的贡献记录和技术能力说明"
msgstr "The nomination must include a record of the candidate's contributions and a description of their technical capabilities."

msgid "现有 `Maintainer` 审阅评估，需 **超过半数当前Maintainer同意且无反对意见**"
msgstr "Existing `Maintainer` review assessment requires **more than half of the current Maintainers to agree with no objections**"

msgid "定期审查"
msgstr "Regular review"

msgid "**每月** 在技术会议上审查所有 `Maintainer` 的活跃情况"
msgstr "**Monthly** review of all `Maintainer` activity at the technical meeting."

msgid "连续 **6 个月** 未对项目做出贡献的 `Maintainer` 可在讨论后转为荣誉身份"
msgstr "A `Maintainer` who has not contributed to the project for **6 consecutive months** may, after discussion, be transitioned to honorary status."

msgid "`荣誉` `Maintainer` 可随时通过恢复活跃贡献申请恢复 `Maintainer` 身份"
msgstr "`Honorary` `Maintainer` can apply to restore their `Maintainer` status at any time by resuming active contributions."
